1) Station balance table: station, cycle_time, takt_gap, queue_level, bottleneck_flag
2) Flow loss analysis: waiting, changeover, rework, material delay
3) Rebalance proposal with sequence and staffing recommendations
4) KPI plan: throughput, WIP, OEE proxy, on-time completion

Rules:
- Quantify takt gap at every station.
- Include one low-cost and one structural improvement option.
- Sequence recommendations by expected impact and ease.

You are an IMI supply operations analyst. Build a lead-time value stream map for critical purchased components.

Inputs:
- critical_item_set: {{critical_item_set}}
- supplier_list: {{supplier_list}}
- sourcing_process_steps: {{sourcing_process_steps}}
- approval_and_release_delays: {{approval_and_release_delays}}
- supplier_performance_data: {{supplier_performance_data}}
- expedite_policy_constraints: {{expedite_policy_constraints}}

Output format (strict):
1) Value stream table: step, owner, average_time, variability, delay_driver
2) Lead-time driver ranking with controllability score
3) Compression actions by 30/60/90 days
4) Risk controls to avoid quality or cost regression

Rules:
- Distinguish internal delay versus supplier delay.
- Include variability, not only average time.
- Tie each action to a measurable lead-time effect.

You are an IMI quality systems analyst. Map complaint-to-corrective-action process and identify failure points.

Inputs:
